{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["Swift"],"name":"Cliques"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjacentPairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacentPairsSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms21AdjacentPairsSequenceV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:ST10AlgorithmsE13adjacentPairsAA08AdjacentC8SequenceVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","title":"adjacentPairs()","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"Swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/adjacentpairs()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjacentPairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms21AdjacentPairsSequenceV","text":"AdjacentPairsSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/adjacentPairs()"},"abstract":[{"text":"Inherited from ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sequence.adjacentPairs()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/adjacentPairs()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/adjacentPairs()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"adjacentPairs"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Algorithms21AdjacentPairsSequenceV","text":"AdjacentPairsSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/adjacentpairs()","title":"adjacentPairs()","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques","kind":"symbol","title":"Cliques","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","abstract":[]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","title":"MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}]}}}